# Keep stray Node tooling out of the Railway upload so Nixpacks doesn't
# auto-detect a Node provider and inject an npm build phase. This is a
# Python (Flask) service started via `bash start_web.sh` (railway.json).
package.json
package-lock.json
node_modules/

# r-connect (2026-06-25): the local tree had grown to 1.2 GB and `railway up`
# was timing out mid-upload. None of the below is built or served at runtime
# (Flask serves only from static/; the git self-heal at main.py:351 is gated
# to REPLIT_ENVIRONMENT and never runs on Railway). Excluding them cuts the
# upload by ~700 MB. Do NOT add routes/, scripts/, static/, or templates/ —
# those ARE imported/served.
.git/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
infrastructure_output/
dchub-frontend/
# ★2026-08-17: docs/brain-proposals/ became a RUNTIME dependency on 08-07 —
# brain_pr_opener.landed_spec_with_fingerprint scans it IN THE IMAGE, and an
# image without it silently blinds spec dedup. GitHub-source builds never read
# this file; these patterns bite only CLI `railway up` uploads — but a single
# CLI deploy with a bare `docs/` exclude would ship a dedup-blind worker.
# Re-including brain-proposals costs ~1 MB of the ~30 MB docs tree. Check the
# "[spec-dedup] corpus at boot" line in deploy logs after any deploy-path change.
docs/*
!docs/brain-proposals/
backups/
